  "comment": "TEST FIXTURE. A synthetic record invented for tests; it describes no real organism, cluster or compound. It covers the cases the real surfactin record does not: medium quality, a hybrid cluster, two compounds, a compound shared with another cluster, a recorded negative bioactivity, cited bioactivities, activity names written as plain text (MIBiG 4.0 uses this style as well as the object style in the surfactin record), one activity object carrying a curator's comment, a compound class, synonyms, a PubChem identifier and a Greek letter in a name. Its gene records (added in Phase 3) cover a RefSeq protein id, locus tags, a gene with no name, a job shown by an activity assay with a reference, a gene with two jobs, a job that does not build the molecule, and a gene record with no identifier. WP_999999901.1 and the TESTI_ locus tags are made up. The 10.0000 DOI prefix belongs to no publisher.",
